1. Open `/controllers/front/OrderConfirmationController.php` and find:

```
public function initContent()
  {
```

2. Add this code:

```
    /* Kelkoo Sales Tracking */
    $order = new Order($this->id_order);
    $products = $order->getProducts();
    $productsKelkoo=array();
    foreach ($products as $product) {
        $productKelkoo=array('productname'=>$product['product_name'],
                             'productid'=>$product['product_reference'],
                             'quantity'=>$product['product_quantity'],
                             'price'=>$product['unit_price_tax_incl']);
        array_push($productsKelkoo,$productKelkoo);
    }
    $this->context->smarty->assign(array(
        'is_guest' => $this->context->customer->is_guest,          
        'HOOK_ORDER_CONFIRMATION' => $this->displayOrderConfirmation(),        
        'HOOK_PAYMENT_RETURN' => $this->displayPaymentReturn(),
        'products_json' => json_encode($productsKelkoo),
        'sales' => $order->getOrdersTotalPaid(),
        'orderid' => $this->id_order
    ));
    /* end Kelkoo Sales Tracking*/
```

3. Go to `themes/custom` (where `custom` is your template name, default "prestashop"), open `order-confirmation.tpl` and add at the bottom:

```
<script type="text/javascript">
    _kkstrack = {
      {literal}merchantInfo: [{ country:"COUNTRY", merchantId:"MERCHANTID_VALUE" }],{/literal}
      orderValue: '{$sales}',
      orderId: '{$orderid}',
      basket: {$products_json}
    };
    (function() {
      var s = document.createElement('script');
      s.type = 'text/javascript';
      s.async = true;
      s.src = 'https://s.kk-resources.com/ks.js';
      var x = document.getElementsByTagName('script')[0];
      x.parentNode.insertBefore(s, x);
    })();
</script>
```

Two things are specific to 1.6: the basket uses `quantity` and `price` keys (1.7 and 8 use `svn1` and `svn2`), and `merchantInfo` is wrapped in `{literal}...{/literal}` tags.

`MERCHANTID_VALUE` and `COUNTRY` can be hard-coded — they are the same for every sale. `COUNTRY` is the 2-letter lower-case country code your products are listed under.

Afterwards clear the cache: **Admin > Advanced Paramaters > Performance > Clear Cache**.

If PayPal payment is enabled on PrestaShop 1.6, two additional files must be changed.

